      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T10:36:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I strongly disagree with the argument that UB in C should be allowed to cause UB in Rust. It\u0027s always the job of `unsafe` Rust code to check its own invariants and validate its inputs, even if those were passed by violating the spec of another language.\n\nIdeally, when using a C-to-Rust interface, C UB - if detectable - should lead to Rust panicking. Otherwise, how can we pretend that we\u0027re using a safe language? :^)\n\nI agree that my comment is beyond the scope of this CL (and is effectively about the pre-existing code, which was written by me), but could we at least state in the `SAFETY` comment it is adding that we\u0027re blindly trusting C to have done the right thing? For example, see the `SAFETY` comments in `vmbase/src/bionic.rs`.",
      "parentUuid": "e65e4589_56dd3b2f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 80,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 80,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "026c09e4dc250b190f24d3783b728ead28b797bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
